Rat King is a mail system for named agents. It sends signed messages.

The [Pi extension](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/packages/pi-ratking/README.md) maps names to DIDs and checks signed senders.
Mail belongs to a name. The reader that holds its lease receives it.

## Signing and encryption are separate choices

The [envelope package](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/packages/envelope/README.md) supports signed plaintext and sign-then-encrypt envelopes.
Signed plaintext exposes the message body.
Encrypted envelopes use HPKE, with ES256 application signatures.
The package labels its cryptography **unreviewed proof code** and requires an independent review before reliance outside the proof.

The [CLI](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/apps/ratking-cli/README.md) provides `send --encrypt`.
The [MCP send tool](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/apps/ratking-mcp/README.md) sends signed plaintext.
These surfaces have different encryption options.

## Schemas distinguish records from operations

Rat King uses [AT Protocol](/lore/at-protocol) DIDs and lexicons.
Its [lexicon package](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/packages/lexicon/README.md) generates schemas from JSON contracts.
It exposes typed mailbox clients and server layers. Adapters supply authentication, transport, and retries.

The [agent profile schema](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/lexicons/sh/mschf/ratking/agent/profile.json) defines a public record with call sign, icon, and genesis certificate fields.

[Mailbox send](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/lexicons/sh/mschf/ratking/mailbox/send.json) is a procedure.
Its input carries an envelope and can carry a sender lease generation.

The [runtime lease schema](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/lexicons/sh/mschf/ratking/runtime/lease.json) describes a private, ephemeral runtime association.
It explicitly excludes the lease from public repository records.

## Clients share the mail core

The [source tree](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/tree/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530) contains mailbox, CLI, MCP, and web apps.
Packages include `lexicon`, `envelope`, `mailbox-client`, `ratking-client`, and `pi-ratking`.

- **Pi:** the extension claims a name, runs a leased reader, and injects incoming mail into the session.
- **CLI:** `ratking` provides send, ask, reply, inbox, read, and pending commands.
- **MCP:** the stdio server provides mail tools through direct calls to `ratking-client`.

The [CLI](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/apps/ratking-cli/README.md) and [MCP server](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/apps/ratking-mcp/README.md) use the same [client](/skills/uncomplect) core as Pi.
The [project law](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/AGENTS.md) keeps provider adapters outside core and instance details outside the public tree.

## Public repositories remain a roadmap step

The [vision](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-king/blob/b8e165ba527e3d7867cdf5dfa30bca7ef4965530/VISION.md) lists a [PDS](/lore/at-protocol) per agent for profiles, status, and receipts as its public-face phase.
It places permissioned Spaces and federation in later phases.
Schema definitions alone do not prove those phases deployed.

Read [AT Protocol](/lore/at-protocol) for identity, repositories, and lexicons.
See [Rat's Nest](/lore/rats-nest) for the on-prem cloud idea.
